Building Neural Nets
The following tips for creating Neural Network will apply whether you choose to use the Pytorch project, or the original one.

Throughout the applications portion of the project, you’ll use the framework provided in nn.py or Pytorch to create neural networks to solve a variety of machine learning problems. A simple neural network has linear layers, where each linear layer performs a linear operation (just like perceptron). Linear layers are separated by a non-linearity, which allows the network to approximate general functions. We’ll use the ReLU operation for our non-linearity, defined as 
